      "post_subject": "Troubleshooting : emulsion peeling off",
      "content_md": "This poor drawing of mine represents my current understanding of the chemistry and over-time phenomena :\n\n![bleach_not_bleached.png](https://holographyforum.org/forum/download/file.php?id=7084)\n\nThere are 2 assumptions that I might have misconception about :\n\n- Isn't light supposed to bounce off the deeper layers of the emulsion to reconstructs the virtual image ? I mean, if there is some black-silver on the way, light would rather probably get absorbed instead of continuing through and bouncing later ?\n\n- Isn't my \"not bleached\" hologram be still sensitive to light at some point ? I mean, if Silver is not removed from the emulsion ?\n\nAgain, a poor but well explanatory drawing :\n\n![bleach_not_bleached_2.png](https://holographyforum.org/forum/download/file.php?id=7083)",
